WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.448
Error handling should help operators understand failures without exposing internals to users.

2
00:00:06.448 --> 00:00:15.962
Production responses should avoid stack traces, internal file paths, dependency versions, database messages, and implementation details.

3
00:00:15.962 --> 00:00:26.028
A user can receive a clear error category and request identifier while the detailed diagnostic information remains in protected operational systems.

4
00:00:26.028 --> 00:00:32.082
Structured logging helps teams search, alert, and investigate behavior across services.

5
00:00:32.082 --> 00:00:43.877
Useful fields may include request IDs, user or tenant identifiers where appropriate, route names, status codes, latency, dependency failures, and security-relevant events.

6
00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:56.537
The logging design should avoid secrets, session tokens, authorization headers, password values, raw sensitive payloads, and personally sensitive data that is not needed for operations.

7
00:00:56.537 --> 00:01:00.547
Observability is also part of incident response readiness.

8
00:01:00.547 --> 00:01:01.491
A Node.

9
00:01:01.491 --> 00:01:16.195
js service should make it possible to notice unusual authentication failures, authorization denials, validation failures, dependency warnings, rate-limit events, unexpected outbound requests, and runtime errors.

10
00:01:16.195 --> 00:01:22.722
Dependency and runtime warnings should not be ignored simply because the service appears to work.

11
00:01:22.722 --> 00:01:25.867
They may signal security or reliability drift.

12
00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:30.900
The balance is to understand behavior without turning logs into a data leak.

13
00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:38.684
Logs often travel to third-party platforms, shared dashboards, long-term storage, backups, or developer laptops.

14
00:01:38.684 --> 00:01:41.515
Treat logs as sensitive operational data.

15
00:01:41.515 --> 00:01:52.917
Good observability helps teams detect and respond to problems while preserving privacy, protecting secrets, and keeping production details out of untrusted responses.
